id: pmc-n07l
title: Read the pm workspace with canonical complete reads instead of default budgets
description: "pm-changelog refuses changelogs generated from partial workspace reads. The changelog-family scripts in package.json invoked pm without --pm-bin and without unbounded output controls, so once this tracker exceeds a single page, changelog gates fail or would silently omit entries on older tool versions. Fix mirrors the pm-beads convention: pin ./node_modules/.bin/pm and request unbounded output."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: changelog,quality-gate
created_at: "2026-08-22T05:37:59.711Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-26T19:15:08.400Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-22T05:38:12.424Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-22T05:38:12.424Z"
author: ox-alpha
acceptance_criteria: "All pm-changelog invocations perform the canonical complete unbounded workspace read; npm run changelog:check exits 0 on this head; no other scripts weakened"
resolution: fixed
expected_result: changelog gates always read the complete tracker and exit 0 whenever the committed changelog matches generated output
actual_result: "Scripts previously used default budgets; after adding --pm-bin and unbounded --pm-arg controls, npm run changelog:check exits 0"
close_reason: "All pm-changelog invocations now perform the canonical complete unbounded workspace read; npm run changelog:check exits 0 on this head."
body: ""
